                    "file": "tools/sdbusplus/templates/event.hpp.mako",
                    "line": 53,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is not correct.  The event file version and the Redfish version are not equivalent.  This is a big part of why I didn't do this in sdbusplus and instead did it in bmcweb.  Only bmcweb has the Redfish Message Registries from the DMTF, so only bmcweb knows the right version."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/sdbusplus/templates/event.hpp.mako",
                    "line": 53,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thang Tran",
                        "email": "thuutran@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "thangtran-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Currently, the bmcweb does not need the version of event. It only need the RegitriesRefix and Event name. I think we can accept this limitation."
                }
